    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a human-readable `telephoneDisplay` field while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164, across three layers:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (the derived-fields block, alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it serializes into the GET response.\n\n2. **`OwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 added a `toDisplay(String e164)` formatter, placed in the existing single-source-of-truth class for the E.164 concept. It splits the known country codes (`+61`, `+1`) off their national part and groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Anything null or not in E.164 form is returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a MapStruct `@Mapping` so `telephoneDisplay` is derived from the stored `owner.getTelephone()`.\n\nSince `telephoneDisplay` is `readOnly`, the inbound `OwnerDto \u2192 Owner` mapping ignores it, and the raw `telephone` remains untouched E.164.",
